WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.987
Professional work also requires a good workflow.

00:00:02.987 --> 00:00:05.212
Git is a version control tool.

00:00:05.212 --> 00:00:08.687
It helps us track changes in a project over time.

00:00:08.687 --> 00:00:14.492
Even if you are working alone, Git is useful because it creates a history of your project.

00:00:14.492 --> 00:00:17.532
A typical workflow has a few steps.

00:00:17.532 --> 00:00:20.107
First, you edit your working files.

00:00:20.107 --> 00:00:23.227
Then you use git status to see what changed.

00:00:23.227 --> 00:00:28.527
Next, you use git add to stage the files you want to include in the next checkpoint.

00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:34.237
Then you use git commit with a message that explains the change.

00:00:34.237 --> 00:00:40.667
Finally, if you are using a remote repository, you use git push to send your commits to that

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:44.477
remote location. A good commit message should describe the purpose of the change.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:48.952
For example, fix missing value handling is more useful than update file.

00:00:48.952 --> 00:00:53.947
You do not need to become a Git expert immediately.

00:00:53.947 --> 00:01:00.397
But you should understand the basic idea: Git helps you save meaningful checkpoints as your project evolves.
